{\f0\fnil Arial;}
{\f1\fnil Symbol;}
{\f2\fnil CG Times;}
}
{\plain {The reason the 1/N appears in the
 IDFT is that, whereas the complex exponential
 sequences are orthogonal, they are not 
orthonormal. Their norm is N and so \{\{ec}{\fs16 
\dn6 n,k }{/sqrt(N)\}\} is an orthonormal
 set of basis vectors. By convention in 
DSP, the DFT is defined with ec not normalized:
 to correct for this the 1/N factor appears
 in the IDFT.}}
}
.TXT 20 0 288 0
Cg a60.250000,62.000000,103
{\rtf1\ansi \deff0
{\fonttbl
{\f0\fnil Arial;}
{\f1\fnil Symbol;}
{\f2\fnil CG Times;}
}
