{\f0\fnil Arial;}
{\f1\fnil Symbol;}
{\f2\fnil CG Times;}
}
{\plain {We now prove}{ that (3.4) is the
 inverse of (3.3). If so, then the DFT operation
 followed by the IDFT operation must be 
the identity operation. Thus, we }{substitute
 (3.3) into the right side of (3.4) and 
show that in fact the sequence \{x}{\fs16 
\dn6 n}{, n=0,...,N-1\} is recovered. Thus
 we want to evaluate the double sum }}
}
