{\plain {Since, by Euler's formula, the 
cosine is expressible as a sum of two conjugate
 exponentials}{, we could have anticipated
 that the DFT would consist of the sum of
 two impulse sequences, one at n = 4 and
 one at n = -4. Because we use the conventional
 indexing from 0 to N-1, and because the
 DFT has period N, this second line appears
 at (-4+N). This is an important observation.}}
}
