{\plain {The phase of a complex number z
 = x+iy is defined when the magnitude z}{\dn8 
m}{ = sqrt(x}{\up8 2}{+y}{\up8 2}{) is not
 zero. Recall that the arctangent(y/x) determines
 an angle in [-}{\f1 p}{/2,}{\f1 p}{/2] 
and  could be used to define the phase of
 the frequency response. However, knowing
 x and y allows us to determine the quadrant
 of z in the complex plane and hence the
 angle in [-}{\f1 p}{,}{\f1 p}{], which 
is more informative. This function is implemented
 as the }{\b arg}{ built-in function in 
Mathcad and gives us a conventionally defined
 phase. However, a still more informative
 definition of the phase is obtained by 
recursively computing the phase differences
 between samples, as follows.}}
}
.TXT 20 -10 366 0
Cg a10.750000,72.000000,35
{\rtf1\ansi \deff0
{\fonttbl
{\f0\fnil Arial;}
{\f1\fnil Symbol;}
{\f2\fnil CG Times;}
