}
{\plain {We show how one can compute the
 DFTs of typical generic sequences using
 Mathcad's symbolic mathematics capability.
 There is a certain art involved in using
 such software. Agreeable forms are sometimes
 obtained only after using the symbolic 
mathematical operations of simplify, factor,
 expand and collect. One must start up the
 symbolic processor by choosing }{\b Load
 Symbolic Processor}{ from the }{\b Symbolic}{
 menu.}}
}
.TXT 14 0 170 0
Cg a61.000000,61.000000,160
{\rtf1\ansi \deff0
{\fonttbl
{\f0\fnil Arial;}
{\f1\fnil Symbol;}
{\f2\fnil CG Times;}
}
{\plain {We begin with a simple sequence,
 namely a geometric series whose sum we 
know. }{We write down a finite geometric
 series in a region of our Mathcad document:}}
}
.EQN 8 17 171 0
((0,{0:N}NAME-1,{0:n}NAME,({0:a}NAME)^({0:n}NAME)){64})
